e-sample-proportion","label":"Check Your Understanding: The Sampling Distribution of the Sample Proportion","html_id":"check-your-understanding-the-sampling-distribution-of-the-sample-proportion","implicit":true,"key":"gaPhkNd0J1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"According to the National Postsecondary Student Aid Study conducted by the U.S. Department of Education in 2008, 62% of graduates from public universities had student loans. Suppose we take random samples of 100 graduates.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"XSx0r77YN6"}],"key":"PytMQtftlz"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-a5666538464903eb44b37d3c2138adaa.mjs","model":{"question":"What are the mean and standard deviation of the sampling distribution of p-hat for samples of size 100?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"Mean 0.62, SD $\\approx 0.049$","feedback":"Correct! Mean = 0.62 and SD = $\\sqrt{0.002356} \\approx 0.049$."},{"correct":false,"text":"Mean 0.5, SD $\\approx 0.049$","feedback":"The mean of the sampling distribution equals the population proportion, 0.62—not 0.5."},{"correct":false,"text":"Mean 0.62, SD $\\approx 0.485$","feedback":"Don't forget to divide by n inside the square root: $\\sqrt{0.62 \\times 0.38/100} \\approx 0.049$."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Mean = p; SD = $\\sqrt{p(1-p)/n} = \\sqrt{0.62 \\times 0.38/100}$.","explanation":""},"key":"FwEvkQhqye"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-a5666538464903eb44b37d3c2138adaa.mjs","model":{"question":"Is it appropriate to describe this sampling distribution as approximately normal?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"Yes—np = 62 and n(1 - p) = 38 both exceed 10","feedback":"Correct! np = 62 and n(1 - p) = 38 are both at least 10, so the normal shape applies."},{"correct":false,"text":"No—the conditions fail","feedback":"Both conditions are satisfied here—recomp